<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agios Kirykos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agios Kirykos is the main town and port of the Greek island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikaria">Ikaria</a> in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>. In July 1912 it was the seat of the provisional government of the short-lived Free State of Icaria, set up after the islanders expelled the Ottoman garrison, before the island joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in November that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agios-kirykos.jpg" alt="Agios Kirykos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stelios Kiousis · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agios_Kirikos,_Ikaria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
